    "notes": "All endpoints the frontend asked for are implemented. Two differences to note: (1) POST .../negotiation/reviews now accepts an OPTIONAL extra request field expectedVersion (number) — when omitted the submission is treated as being on the latest version and NO 409 is raised, so the UI must send expectedVersion to get the stale-redline 409; (2) settings audit log entries use logAction constrained to exactly 'Created'|'Updated'|'Deleted' (enum), and the settings paged response class is named AuditLogListResponse with items/page/pageSize/totalCount. Both audit logs are now append-only: PUT/PATCH/DELETE on /api/v1/settings/audit-log/{entryId} and /api/v1/lifecycle/contracts/{contractId}/audit-log/{entryId} return 403 with error/details 'Audit log entries cannot be modified or deleted.' (not 405). GET .../negotiation and compare return 404 when no routing exists; accept-suggestion/PUT clause/reject all return the full ClauseResponse (superset of the fields the frontend listed). GET .../negotiation/compare requires versionA and versionB as mandatory query params — omitting them is a 400. Role lists are narrower than the frontend may assume: routing/reminder POSTs are CONTRACT_OWNER only, PUT clause/reject/mark-agreed are LEGAL_REVIEWER only, and all /api/v1/settings/audit-log access is TENANT_ADMIN only."
  },
